"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/3049620/extras/bd3a5b7bd016129c4b30ed5143fad40a.webm?t=1772479851\" type=\"video/webm; codecs=vp9\"><source src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/3049620/extras/bd3a5b7bd016129c4b30ed5143fad40a.mp4?t=1772479851\" type=\"video/mp4\"></video></span></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >In the <strong>Convoy Campaign</strong> you need to strike a balance between developing your colony and your fleet. Length and difficulty settings define how many people you need to save to achieve victory. Lifeboats are sourced from your army, thus weakening you in missions. Along the way, you unlock technologies which you may take with you on your next run\u2014should this one fail.</p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >Colony</h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Grow your colony by constructing buildings with special roles and benefits. Each building is limited by charges, which restricts expansion. Deconstructing a building improves the underlying tile and returns a charge. You are tasked with completing a set of goals, but this is your safe space. Here you may concentrate on building the most efficient colonies you can think of.</p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >Boss Battle</h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><video class=\"bb_img\" autoplay muted loop playsinline poster=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/3049620/extras/414d11bbf5930ccde589a9b93b95f87a.poster.avif?t=1772479851\" width=426 height=240 ><source src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/3049620/extras/414d11bbf5930ccde589a9b93b95f87a.webm?t=1772479851\" type=\"video/webm; codecs=vp9\"><source src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/3049620/extras/414d11bbf5930ccde589a9b93b95f87a.mp4?t=1772479851\" type=\"video/mp4\"></video></span></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >There is a dedicated game mode in which you will face bosses. The whole map will try to defeat you, so it may be wise to either rush the boss or dismantle their production facilities. Additionally, you may design your own boss and battle against preset or community bosses. Winning in &quot;Boss Versus Boss&quot; battles improves your score. Currently, your last boss is uploaded to the leaderboard and becomes available as an encounter for other players.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Key Features:</strong>  </p><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" > Lane-pushing strategy with modular, auto-firing capital ships </p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" > Multiple game modes and maps with shifting rules and objectives </p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" > Two distinct campaigns with persistent progression systems </p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" > Colony building as a safe space during campaigns and as a standalone skirmish </p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" > Custom boss creation </p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" > Focus on <strong>Singleplayer</strong> but with Multiplayer support </p></li></ul><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >Is This Game for You? </h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Breeze of Ashes is for players who enjoy strategic planning, systems that stack and interact, and making meaningful choices under pressure. If you like lane-pushing gameplay, asymmetric factions, and campaigns that reward long-term thinking, you will feel at home. </p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >If you are looking for a pure action game, a traditional RTS with full micromanagement, or a purely narrative experience, this may not be the right fit. </p>","developers":["Chocolate Ship Games"],"genres":[{"description":"Indie","id":"23"},{"description":"Strategy","id":"2"}],"header_image":"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/3049620/48d9fc6ebb4074999f4f27acbf275cc4c1df9e67/header.jpg?t=1772479851","is_free":false,"linux_requirements":{"minimum":"<strong>Minimum:</strong><br><ul class=\"